rces them to find moves elsewhere, likely pushing them to less optimal outer squares.\n\nReason: Move (F, 3) is the most strategic choice. It adheres to the strategy of "mobility" by making a quiet move that limits the changes to the board, preserving my options while denying the opponent easy targets. It builds a stable base on Row F and avoids the risks associated with extending to the B or G rows.\n\nAnswer: (F, 3)'}
